{{!-- primitive-chart — @mui/x-charts line/bar chart over a grouped
  projection's LIST response (M-T1.3).

  x-charts is MUI's own charting package, so it reads the active MUI theme for
  its series colour, axis ink and grid — no colour is passed here on purpose.
  That keeps the chart on the pack's palette (including its dark mode) and
  leaves the per-pack WCAG-AA contrast gate reasoning about one set of tokens
  rather than a chart-only palette.

  x-charts binds data differently from recharts: rows go to `dataset`, the
  category axis names its column via `dataKey`, and each series names its
  measure the same way.  The axis `scaleType` differs by kind — `point` for a
  line (values sit ON the tick) and `band` for bars (each bar occupies a slot).

  A chart is an image of data, so the wrapper carries `role="img"` plus the
  walker-derived `aria-label` (same contract as primitive-data-grid).  One
  series, so the legend is off: the label names the measure already. --}}
    <div role="img" aria-label="{{ariaLabel}}"{{{testidAttr}}}>
{{#if isLine}}      <LineChart dataset={ {{{dataExpr}}} } xAxis={[{ dataKey: "{{dataKey}}", scaleType: "point" }]} series={[{ dataKey: "{{seriesField}}" }]} height={300} hideLegend />
{{else}}      <BarChart dataset={ {{{dataExpr}}} } xAxis={[{ dataKey: "{{dataKey}}", scaleType: "band" }]} series={[{ dataKey: "{{seriesField}}" }]} height={300} hideLegend />
{{/if}}    </div>
